agm-0973: AGM H6 GPU pool. The ADT gives the kernel 4.75 GB (mkadt.py AGM_MEM_SIZE 0x130000000);
the top 1.25 GB of DRAM (0x2_30000000-0x2_80000000) is TopazAdreno.cpp's GPU pool on AGM,
write-combined and never in the processors' caches. AgmMaliGPU takes Mesa's buffers from it
(cached buffers only for the tiler heap and when the pool is full), SweetSurface the window
server's screen-sized surfaces (agm_gpu=1, 720x1600 and up); neither is flushed at submissions
nor invalidated before the display shows it. SweetFramebuffer shows pool frames directly only
where there is an MDP (fCtl0; NULL on AGM: data abort at 0x18), else copies them.
AgmMaliGPU logs flush statistics every 5 s.

